From 98b4f17d202f3dd732fc18a26a437f34d4edbc25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lotus V2 Review <v2-review@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:46:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add parameterized V2 monetary and resource arithmetic

Implement the P06 bootstrap reserve and work-responsive tail recurrence with exact wide integer arithmetic over the existing 56-byte MonetaryState. Add P05 parabolic transaction/block costs, frozen-accounting EMA, stricter enforcement burn floor, and C16 fee split, token burn, coinbase entitlement, mandatory underclaim, explicit burn and spendable supply delta.

The API requires a caller-selected development profile and independently validated transaction fees, block costs, coinbase outputs and envelope bytes. It does not parse or connect blocks, freeze production constants, select payouts or persist undo state. Test hand-derived boundaries and 300 differential vectors against the separately maintained Python reference in Debug and Release.
